WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.114
<v Examiner>Three marks.

2
00:00:02.114 --> 00:00:07.277
<v Examiner>Describe salbutamol: its class, how it works, and what the nurse teaches about using it.

3
00:00:07.727 --> 00:00:10.514
Class: salbutamol is a bronchodilator.

4
00:00:10.514 --> 00:00:12.055
It opens the airways.

5
00:00:12.055 --> 00:00:17.263
More exactly, it's a short-acting beta-2 agonist, the reliever inhaler.

6
00:00:17.713 --> 00:00:22.872
How it works: it binds to beta-2 receptors in the smooth muscle of the airways,

7
00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:26.921
which relaxes the muscle and opens the airways within minutes.

8
00:00:26.921 --> 00:00:31.296
That makes it the textbook agonist: it binds and causes a response.

9
00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:36.913
The opposite is a beta blocker like metoprolol, an antagonist, which binds and blocks.

10
00:00:37.363 --> 00:00:41.094
Use: asthma and C O P D, for wheeze and breathlessness.

11
00:00:41.094 --> 00:00:45.640
Side effects: tremor, a fast heart rate, palpitations and headache.

12
00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:51.444
What the nurse teaches: how to use the inhaler with a spacer; to carry it at all times;

13
00:00:51.444 --> 00:00:56.122
and that needing it more and more often means their asthma isn't controlled,

14
00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.229
so see the doctor.

15
00:00:57.229 --> 00:01:02.768
And what the nurse assesses before and after: respiratory rate, work of breathing, wheeze,

16
00:01:02.768 --> 00:01:04.799
oxygen saturation and heart rate.

17
00:01:05.249 --> 00:01:10.359
Salbutamol: a bronchodilator, a short-acting beta-2 agonist, the reliever.

18
00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:15.262
Binds beta-2 receptors, relaxes airway smooth muscle, works in minutes.

19
00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:16.574
Asthma and C O P D.

20
00:01:16.574 --> 00:01:19.198
Side effects: tremor, fast heart rate.

21
00:01:19.198 --> 00:01:23.411
Teach the spacer; needing it more often means see the doctor.

22
00:01:23.411 --> 00:01:27.692
Assess breathing, saturations and heart rate before and after.
